.\" Author: Vasiliy Zdanovskiy <vasilyvz@gmail.com>
.TH MCP-TERMINAL-CONFIG 5 "@VERSION@" "mcp-terminal-docker" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
mcp-terminal-config \- MCP Terminal term server JSON configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
The MCP Terminal service reads a single JSON file in SimpleConfig shape
(compatible with \fBmcp-proxy-adapter\fR). On a production host installed via
the \fBmcp-terminal-docker\fR package the active file is:
.PP
.RS
.B /etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json
.RE
.PP
It is a \fIconffile\fR: package upgrades do not overwrite an existing file.
The seed template is also shipped as
.IR /usr/share/mcp-terminal/term_server.json .
.PP
Inside the Docker container the same file is mounted read-only at
.IR /etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json .
.PP
Validate syntax and cross-field rules before restart (inside the container or
dev venv with \fBmcp-terminal\fR installed):
.PP
.RS
.EX
python3 -m mcp_terminal.config.config_cli validate -c /etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json
.EE
.RE
.PP
After edits: \fBsudo mcp-terminal-docker recreate\fR.
.SH PRODUCTION PLACEHOLDERS
On first install the package seeds \fB/etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json\fR from
\fB/usr/share/mcp-terminal/term_server.json.template\fR with placeholders that
must be replaced before the service starts (same convention as casmgr-server):
.TP
.B CHANGE_ME
\fBserver.advertised_host\fR — this host's IP or DNS name for MCP proxy registration.
.TP
.B MCP_PROXY_HOST
\fBregistration.register_url\fR, \fBunregister_url\fR, \fBheartbeat.url\fR — MCP proxy hostname/IP.
.TP
.B REPLACE_ON_INSTALL
\fBregistration.instance_uuid\fR — replaced with a new UUID4 on first install by
\fBinstall-server-config.sh\fR.
.TP
.B CODE_ANALYSIS_HOST
\fBcode_analysis.host\fR when \fBcode_analysis.enabled\fR is true — hostname or IP of
\fBcasmgr-server\fR (production package port \fB15010\fR; dev checkout \fB15000\fR).
.TP
.B WATCH_DIRS_ROOT
\fBwatch_dirs.directories\fR — parent directory whose subdirectories are project roots.
Must be bind-mounted into the service container via \fBMCP_TERMINAL_EXTRA_BINDS\fR
in \fI/etc/default/mcp-terminal\fR (same host path inside the container).
.PP
The service and \fBmcp-terminal-docker.service\fR will not start while any placeholder
remains. After edits: \fBsudo mcp-terminal-docker recreate\fR.
.SH EXECUTION MODES
Two command paths share sessions and shell state but differ in where processes run:
.TP
.B terminal_run
Container/sandbox execution. Uses \fBruntime\fR (image profile, network, limits) and
spawns per-session Docker containers on the host daemon (via mounted \fBdocker.sock\fR).
.TP
.B terminal_run_host
Host execution. Uses \fBterminal.host_execution\fR (\fBenabled\fR plus
\fBallowed_commands\fR allowlist). Commands run directly on the host filesystem
outside session containers — use only when sandbox isolation is not required.
.PP
Configure both sections in production; disable \fBhost_execution.enabled\fR or empty
the allowlist to reject all host-side runs.
.SH PRODUCTION PATHS
.TP
.B Configuration
.RS
/etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json
.RE
.TP
.B TLS certificates (server HTTPS)
.RS
/etc/mcp-terminal/mtls_certificates/
.br
In JSON use absolute container paths, e.g.
.BR /etc/mcp-terminal/mtls_certificates/server/mcp-proxy.pem
for server cert/key and
.BR /etc/mcp-terminal/mtls_certificates/mtls_certificates/client/mcp-proxy.crt
for outbound client TLS to the MCP proxy.
.RE
.TP
.B Logs
.RS
Host: \fB/var/log/mcp-terminal/\fR → container \fB/var/log/mcp-terminal\fR
.br
Set \fBserver.log_dir\fR to \fB/var/log/mcp-terminal\fR in JSON.
.RE
.TP
.B Data
.RS
Host: \fB/var/mcp-terminal/\fR → container \fB/var/mcp-terminal\fR
.RE
.SH TOP-LEVEL SECTIONS
.TP
.B server
(required) Listen address (\fB0.0.0.0\fR inside container), port (\fB3011\fR),
\fBadvertised_host\fR (IP or hostname registered with MCP proxy), \fBprotocol\fR
(\fBhttps\fR in production), \fBservername\fR (TLS SNI), \fBlog_dir\fR.
.TP
.B registration
Proxy registration. When \fBenabled\fR is true, set \fBregister_url\fR,
\fBunregister_url\fR, \fBheartbeat.url\fR, \fBserver_id\fR, \fBserver_name\fR.
Use \fBregistration.ssl\fR for outbound TLS to the proxy.
.TP
.B queue_manager
Job queue for terminal commands (\fBenabled\fR, \fBmax_concurrent_jobs\fR, etc.).
.TP
.B watch_dirs
Project registry refresh: \fBdirectories\fR (host paths that must be bind-mounted
into the service container via \fBMCP_TERMINAL_EXTRA_BINDS\fR in
.IR /etc/default/mcp-terminal ),
\fBrefresh_interval_seconds\fR.
.TP
.B terminal
Terminal domain: session TTL, output limits, cleanup, admin flags, and
\fBhost_execution\fR (allowlist for \fBterminal_run_host\fR).
.TP
.B runtime
Sandbox defaults for \fBterminal_run\fR: image profile, network mode, timeouts,
resource limits, concurrent run cap.
.TP
.B code_analysis
Client to \fBcasmgr-server\fR for project registry refresh via \fBwatch_dirs\fR.
When \fBenabled\fR is true, set \fBhost\fR and \fBport\fR (production \fB15010\fR).
.SH SANDBOX IMAGES
Session containers use pre-published worker images on Docker Hub (default
\fB<user>/mcp-terminal-python-dev:3.12\fR, \fB<user>/mcp-terminal-node-dev:20\fR,
\fB<user>/mcp-terminal-base-tools:latest\fR). The package pulls these on install/upgrade; paths in
project registry must exist on the \fBhost\fR Docker daemon (bind-mount the same
paths into the service container).
.SH EXAMPLE (PRODUCTION FRAGMENTS)
.nf
{
  "server": {
    "host": "0.0.0.0",
    "port": 3011,
    "protocol": "https",
    "log_dir": "/var/log/mcp-terminal",
    "advertised_host": "192.168.1.10"
  },
  "registration": {
    "enabled": true,
    "register_url": "https://PROXY:3004/register",
    "server_id": "mcp-terminal"
  },
  "watch_dirs": {
    "directories": ["/home/projects"],
    "refresh_interval_seconds": 60
  },
  "queue_manager": { "enabled": true, "max_concurrent_jobs": 10 }
}
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json
Active configuration (conffile).
.TP
.B /etc/default/mcp-terminal
Host Docker settings (port, paths, networks, extra binds); not the service JSON.
.TP
.B /usr/share/mcp-terminal/term_server.json.template
Package seed template (placeholders CHANGE_ME, MCP_PROXY_HOST, CODE_ANALYSIS_HOST,
WATCH_DIRS_ROOT).
